<% title "Learn | Fuime" %>

<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="description" content="How to start and run a small business: finding something people will pay for, setting a price, working out whether the numbers add up, getting customers and keeping them.">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="Fuime">
  <meta property="og:title" content="How to start and run a small business">
  <meta property="og:url" content="<%= learn_url %>">
<% end %>

<%# Fuime: /learn. See LearnController for why this is public and indexable.

    Two rules this page shares with everything else that touches pricing:
    nothing here names a number a founder should charge, and nothing here ranks
    one template above another. The templates are in Fuime::ServiceCatalog's own
    order and the lessons are in Fuime::Playbook's — no "most popular", no
    "recommended", because a platform that recommends is a platform that
    directs (§8.3 D2). %>

<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto py-8 px-4">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">How to start and run a small business</h1>
    <p class="muted m-0 max-w-2xl">
      Seven lessons on how businesses actually work, and ten starter templates
      for things you could begin this month. Written for people starting their
      first one, with nothing assumed.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%# ── Templates ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-1" id="templates">Start from a template</h2>
  <p class="muted mt-0 mb-4 max-w-2xl">
    Ten businesses you could actually run. Each one covers what to offer, where
    the first customers come from, and the mistakes that are specific to that
    trade. What to charge is left to you, because your costs are not anybody
    else's.
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
    <% @services.each do |service| %>
      <%= link_to learn_template_path(slug: service.key, venture: @venture&.slug),
                  class: "card flex flex-col gap-1 no-underline" do %>
        <strong class="block"><%= service.name %></strong>
        <p class="m-0 text-sm muted"><%= service.blurb %></p>
        <% if service.offer_ideas.present? %>
          <span class="text-sm mt-1">
            <%= pluralize(service.offer_ideas.length, "thing") %> to list &rarr;
          </span>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# ── Lessons ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-1" id="lessons">The lessons</h2>
  <p class="muted mt-0 mb-4 max-w-2xl">
    These work the same whether you mow lawns or edit video. If you have never
    run anything before, read them in order. They are written in the order the
    questions actually turn up.
  </p>

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 mb-10">
    <% @lessons.each_with_index do |lesson, index| %>
      <%= link_to learn_lesson_path(slug: lesson.key, venture: @venture&.slug),
                  class: "card flex items-start gap-4 no-underline" do %>
        <span class="muted text-lg font-bold shrink-0 w-6 text-right"><%= index + 1 %></span>
        <span class="min-w-0">
          <strong class="block"><%= lesson.title %></strong>
          <span class="text-sm muted"><%= lesson.blurb %></span>
        </span>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# ── Where to go next ───────────────────────────────────────────────── %>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-1" id="resources">The rest of it</h2>
  <p class="muted mt-0 mb-4 max-w-2xl">
    The things people ask about next.
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-10">
    <%# Deliberately the real pages rather than a summary of them: the FAQ and
        the Guardian Agreement are the documents a parent is actually asked to
        accept, and a learn-page paraphrase of a legal document is a second
        version of it that nobody updates. %>
    <div class="card">
      <strong class="block mb-1">Why a parent has to be on your account</strong>
      <p class="text-sm muted m-0 mb-2">
        Under 18, a contract you sign can be cancelled at your own option. That
        is why almost nobody will open an account for you, and why a guardian's
        signature is what makes your business real to the people you deal with.
      </p>
      <%= link_to "Read the FAQ", faq_path, class: "text-sm underline" %>
      &middot;
      <%= link_to "The Guardian Agreement", guardian_agreement_path, class: "text-sm underline" %>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <strong class="block mb-1">See what other people are running</strong>
      <p class="text-sm muted m-0 mb-2">
        The fastest way to understand what a finished business looks like is to
        look at some. Every one in the directory is run by somebody your age.
      </p>
      <%= link_to "Open the directory", fuime_directory_path, class: "text-sm underline" %>
    </div>

    <% if @venture.present? %>
      <div class="card">
        <strong class="block mb-1">Your own business</strong>
        <p class="text-sm muted m-0 mb-2">
          What <%= @venture.name %> sells, and what it might owe at tax time.
        </p>
        <%= link_to "What you sell", fuime_offers_path(event_slug: @venture.slug), class: "text-sm underline" %>
        &middot;
        <%= link_to "Tax Tracker", fuime_taxes_path(event_slug: @venture.slug), class: "text-sm underline" %>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <div class="card">
        <strong class="block mb-1">Ready to start one</strong>
        <p class="text-sm muted m-0 mb-2">
          Applying takes a few minutes. You pick what you do, describe it in a
          sentence, and invite the parent or guardian who signs for it.
        </p>
        <%= link_to "Start a business", apply_path, class: "text-sm underline" %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
